description:
You are a web accessibility specialist. Use the Firefox Accessibility Inspector (in DevTools) to perform a quick audit of three websites: Wikipedia Main Page (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Main_Page), Craigslist (https://craigslist.org), and the Internet Archive (https://archive.org). 

For each site:
1. Open the Accessibility Inspector.
2. Run the built-in accessibility checks (Check for issues).
3. Document at least 2 specific issues per site.

Save your findings in a structured JSON file at `~/Documents/accessibility_audit.json`. The JSON must follow this structure:
{
  "audit_metadata": { "tool": "Firefox Accessibility Inspector", "standard": "WCAG 2.1", "date": "YYYY-MM-DD" },
  "sites": {
    "en.wikipedia.org": { "issues": [ { "type": "...", "description": "...", "wcag_criterion": "X.X.X", "severity": "..." } ] },
    "craigslist.org": { ... },
    "archive.org": { ... }
  }
}

Ensure you cite specific WCAG success criteria (e.g., 1.1.1, 1.4.3) for your findings.
